Refactor the Helenize deploy mechanism so its generated artifacts use the REAL native opencode formats. This is a surgical fix with a complete diagnosis already made. Do NOT invent formats — follow exactly the official opencode docs patterns below.

## Background (verified facts)
- opencode version 1.18.11. Native plugin discovery: files in `~/.config/opencode/plugins/` are auto-loaded at startup.
- Native agent format (official docs): markdown file in `~/.config/opencode/agents/<name>.md` with frontmatter keys only: description (required), mode (primary|subagent|all), model, temperature, steps, disable, prompt, tools, permission, hidden, color, top_p. `tools` is a BOOLEAN MAP (e.g. `bash: true`), NEVER a YAML list. Unknown frontmatter keys make the whole config INVALID.
- Native plugin format (official docs): a module exporting NAMED async functions: `export const MyPlugin = async ({ project, client, $, directory, worktree }) => { ... return { "hook.name": async (input, output) => {...} } }`. Hooks include: `session.created`, `session.idle`, `tool.execute.before`, `tool.execute.after`, `shell.env`, `todo.updated`, `command.executed`, `permission.asked`, `experimental.session.compacting`. There is NO `export default { id, deploy }` and NO `api.sidebar.register` — these are wrong.
- Current broken state (must fix): `~/.config/opencode/agents/onp-spec-driven.md` (and the 11 sibling helenized agents) have `mode: primary`, `tools:` as a list, and `origin:`/`tags:` in frontmatter → `opencode debug config` fails with "Configuration is invalid at .../onp-spec-driven.md" and `opencode run` exits 1. The generated plugins use the fake `export default { id, deploy }` format.
- The generator is `/mnt/dados/harness/autofagia/helenize_deploy.py` (read it). It writes: skills to `~/.opencode/skills/<slug>/SKILL.md`, subagents to `~/.config/opencode/agents/<slug>.md`, hooks to `~/.config/opencode/hooks/helenize-<slug>.sh`, plugins to `~/.config/opencode/plugins/<slug>/index.ts`, plus upserts registry at `/mnt/dados/opencode/config/agents/gran-mestre/agent-registry.json`. Alvos spec: `/mnt/dados/harness/autofagia/alvos.json`, catalog: `/mnt/dados/harness/autofagia/catalogo-padroes.json`.

## Tasks (in order)

### 1. Fix `subagent_md()` in the generator
New frontmatter must be exactly:
```
---
description: <single-line description mentioning the absorbed repo>
mode: subagent
tools:
  bash: true
  read: true
  edit: true
  webfetch: true
---
```
- Remove `origin:`, `tags:`, `mode: primary`. Move the origin info into the body (e.g. `## Origem` section with the repo URL). Keep description single-line (no folded `>-` scalars). The body keeps the scope/patterns/rules content that is already generated.

### 2. Fix `plugin_ts()` in the generator
Generate a real native plugin per alvo:
```ts
// Helen {
// plugin helenizado de <repo> — gerado por helenize_deploy.py (NÃO editar)
// Formato nativo opencode: export const <Name> = async (ctx) => ({ hooks })
export const Helenize<Name> = async ({ client, $ }) => {
  // telemetria leve: registra sessão criada com origem do framework absorvido
  return {
    "session.created": async (input) => {
      // no-op leve; o registro de origem vive no agent-registry (consulta via gran-mestre arsenal)
    },
  };
};
```
- `<Name>` = PascalCase slug. Must compile as valid TS with `deno check` (the project uses `deno check` for validation). Do NOT import anything exotic — plain TS only.
- If a plugin file is trivial/no-op, that is fine — the registry is the real source of truth.

### 3. Create the global boot plugin
Create `~/.config/opencode/plugins/gran-mestre-boot/index.ts` (or a single file `~/.config/opencode/plugins/gran-mestre-boot.ts` — check which layout opencode actually auto-loads: the existing working plugins are in subdirectories `plugins/<name>/index.ts`, so use that layout) with native format:
```ts
